[CR CR0341r1 for 37.340] Reason for change: The typo “Modication” in figures 10.2.1-1, 10.2.2-1, 10.7.2-1, 10.8.1-1, and 10.8.2-1 should be fixed. X2AP messages should be used in section 10.7.1. For “NOTE 1a: In case the handover is a conditional handover, step 3a and step 3b are performed after the source MN receives an indication that the UE has successfully accessed one of the potential target eNB as described in TS 36.300 [2], (i.e. after step 6)” in section 10.8.1, it is unclear whether the step 6 refers to the Figure 10.1.2.1a-1 in TS 36.300 or Figure 10.7.1-1 in TS 37.340. The same issue also exists in section 10.8.2. Various editorial corrections should be fixed. Summary of change: Fix the typo in figures 10.2.1-1, 10.2.2-1, 10.7.2-1, 10.8.1-1, and 10.8.2-1. Fix the message “SN Addition Request (Acknowledge)” to “SgNB Addition Request (Acknowledge)” and “SN Release Request” to “SgNB Release Request” in section 10.7.1. Update the text “... after the source MN receives an indication that the UE has successfully accessed one of the potential target eNB(s) as described in step 11a in Figure 10.1.2.1a-1 in TS 36.300 [2], i.e. after step 6 in Figure 10.8.1-1.” for NOTE 1a in section 10.8.1, and the text “... after the source MN receives an indication that the UE has successfully accessed one of the potential target gNB(s) as described in step 8a in Figure 9.2.3.4.2-1 in TS 38.300 [3], i.e. after step 6 in Figure 10.8.2-1.” for NOTE 1a in section 10.8.2. Fix some editorial changes in section 10.2. Impact analysis Impacted 5G architecture options: (NG)EN-DC, NR-DC, NE-DC Impacted functionality: MR-DC operation Inter-operability: If the network implements the CR and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue. If the UE implements the CR and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue. Consequences if not approved: The message name in some texts and figures are incorrect.
